  "text": "Aeracura, also named Aericura or Heracura, was a Celtic goddess. People worshipped her in Germany and Switzerland. She stood as the partner of Dis Pater. Her name resembles that of the Greek goddess Hecate, so scholars link them. Art shows her holding a cornucopia. That emblem stands for fruitfulness and for the Otherworld. The book also places her with the Deae Matres.",
